OL,3,AMPs to vote on bill to legalise
OL,4,Aassisted dying in England and Wales
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt's the second attempt to change the
OL,7,Flaw - last year an identical bill was
OL,8,Fsupported by MPs, but stalled and ran
OL,9,Fout of time in the House of Lords
OL,11,FBoth sides expect the result to be
OL,12,Fclose - one person closely involved
OL,13,Ftells the BBC: "It's on a knife edge"
OL,15,FIf MPs pass the bill today - and it
OL,16,Fcompletes its passage through the
OL,17,FCommons without any changes - then the
OL,18,FLords cannot halt its progress a second
OL,19,Ftime
OL,23,APub: 11-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/38
